### 1. Validation policy: unconditional parser revalidation, policy remains semantic-only

Choose the third option: phase-separated validation.

- Keep `parse_process_ir_v1(payload: Any) -> ProcessIRV1` unchanged. Do not add `validation_policy`.
- Every direct `compile_process_ir_v1(...)` call, including policy-bearing legacy calls, must first serialize the supplied mutable model with `model_dump(mode="json", warnings=False)` and reparse it strictly.
- `LegacyValidationPolicyV1` continues to apply only after CFG lowering, when `_enforce_semantic_report` reclassifies named semantic findings.
- A parser-invalid legacy model is therefore refused with the parser’s diagnostic even when a legacy policy is supplied. Legacy callers retain their deliberate semantic exemptions, but no longer retain divergent grammar diagnostics.

Evidence:

- ProcessIR models are mutable because `_ProcessIRBase` forbids extras but is not frozen: [process_ir.py](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/models/process_ir.py:190), lines 190–194.
